      "message": "Using bootchart, it looks like init had a +43ms / 3% increase (I only ran it once before/after the change on `aosp_cf_x86_64_phone-trunk_staging-userdebug` on `git_main` on an android virtual device).\n\n```\n$ compare-bootcharts.py ~/android-bootchart2 ~/android-bootchart-changes\nprocess: baseline experiment (delta)\n - Unit is ms (a jiffy is 8 ms on the system)\n------------------------------------\n/system/bin/init: 1408 1452 (+43)\n/system/bin/surfaceflinger: 10530 10304 (-226)\n/system/bin/bootanimation: 12043 11878 (-165)\nzygote64: 9147 8947 (-200)\nzygote: 9156 8956 (-200)\nsystem_server: 14878 14547 (-330)\nbootanimation ends at: 24069 23278 (-791)\n```\n\nConsidering https://source.android.com/docs/core/perf/boot-times as a frame of reference, this seems like a reasonable increase, but I\u0027m certainly not well-versed in boot time.",
